          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Semi-topological K-theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi K
                    %mo *
                    %mi st
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_*^{st}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+theory"} homological invariant
            of complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+spaces"} noncommutative spaces
            that interpolates between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonconnective+algebraic+K-theory"} nonconnective algebraic K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+topology"} etale
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-sheaf"} sheaf
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi A
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}^1
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+invariant"} homotopy invariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            from this by inverting the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bott+element"} Bott element
          %p
            Semi-topological K-theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+varieties"} complex varieties
            is related to
            %span.newWikiWord
              morphic cohomology
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/morphic+cohomology"} ?
            in the same way that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            is related to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+cohomology"} motivic cohomology
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            is related to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+cohomology"} singular cohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-Hirzebruch+spectral+sequence"} Atiyah-Hirzebruch spectral sequence
          %p
            Some
            %a{:href => "#Examples"} examples
            suggest that semi-topological K-theory may be a better suited invariant for complex varieties than either algebraic or topological K-theory.
          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong> (topological realization of presheaves)
              \. Taking underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              of complex points induces a functor of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-categories"} infinity-categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Aff
                      %mi C
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Spc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |-| : Aff_C \longrightarrow Spc
            %p
              from complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+schemes"} affine schemes
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Kan+extension"} left Kan extension
              it extends to a
              = succeed "-preserving" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo :
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Aff
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Spc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |-| : P(Aff_\mathbf{C}) \longrightarrow Spc
            %p
              on the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-category+of+infinity-presheaves"} infinity-category of infinity-presheaves
              = succeed "-preserving" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mi Spt
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Aff
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Spt
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |-| : P^{Spt}(Aff_\mathbf{C}) \longrightarrow Spt
            %p
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-category"} infinity-category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-presheaf"} presheaves
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Kan+extension"} left Kan extension
              of the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Aff
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi Spc
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Σ
                          %mn ∞
                    %mi Spt
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(Aff_\mathbf{C}) \stackrel{|-|}{\longrightarrow} Spc \stackrel{\Sigma^{\infty}}{\longrightarrow} Spt
            %p
              along the canonical functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Aff
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mi Spt
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Aff
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(Aff_\mathbf{C}) \to P^{Spt}(Aff_\mathbf{C})
              induced by taking
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectra"} suspension spectra
              objectwise.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-category"} dg-category
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(T)
            denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-connective+algebraic+K-theory"} nonconnective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+K-theory+of+a+dg-category"} Waldhausen K-theory
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-presheaf"} presheaf
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Aff
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Spt
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(T \otimes_{\mathbf{C}} -) : Aff_C^{op} \longrightarrow Spt
          %p
            which sends
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(A)
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(T \otimes_{\mathbf{C}} A)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong semi-topological K-theory
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
              defined by the formula
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mi st
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi et
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{st}(T) = |L^{A^1}(L^{et}(K(T \otimes_{\mathbf{C}} -)))|
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi et
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^{et}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^{A^1}
              are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+topology"} etale
              and
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi A
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}^1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+invariant"} homotopy invariant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} localization
              endofunctors, respectively.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong semi-topological K-theory
              of a complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mi st
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mi st
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Perf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{st}(T) = K^{st}(Perf(X))
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Perf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Perf(X)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-category"} dg-category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perfect+complexes"} perfect complexes
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-category"} dg-category
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_T
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+moduli+stack+of+objects+in+a+dg-category"} moduli space of pseudo-perfect dg-modules
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+stack"} derived stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stack"} infinity-stack
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-category"} infinity-category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+commutative+rings"} simplicial commutative rings
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+commutative+rings"} simplicial commutative rings
            in the obvious way), one gets a spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\mathcal{M}_T|
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\mathcal{M}_T|
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+loop+space"} infinite loop space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi st
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{K}^{st}(T) \simeq |\mathcal{M}_T|
            %p
              where the left hand side is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connective+spectrum"} connective
              version of semi-topological K-theory.
          %p
            See (
            %a{:href => "#Blanc13"}> Blanc 13
            , 4.3), (
            %a{:href => "#Toen10"}> Toen 10
            ), (
            %a{:href => "#Kaledin10"}> Kaledin 10
            , section 8).
          %h2#conjectures Conjectures
          .num_conjecture
            %h6#conjecture Conjecture
            %p
              %strong> (lattice conjecture)
              \. For every smooth proper
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-category"} dg-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ch
                      %mi top
                    %msub
                      %mo ∧
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi S
                    %mi H
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mi top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ∧
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi S
                    %mi H
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi HP
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ch^{top} \wedge_{\mathbf{S}} H \mathbf{C}
                    \: K^{top}(T) \wedge_{\mathbf{S}} H\mathbf{C}
                    \\longrightarrow HP(T)
            %p
              induced by the noncommutative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
              is an equivalence of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
          %p
            (move this to
            = succeed "\u2026)" do
              %span.newWikiWord
                topological K-theory of a dg-category
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/topological+K-theory+of+a+dg-category"} ?
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                On a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mi st
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Spec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mi top
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Spec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{st}(\Spec(\mathbf{C})) \simeq K^{top}(\Spec(\mathbf{C})),
              %p
                while the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
                are uncountable in degree
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \gt 0
            %li
              %p
                With finite
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi K
                        %mo *
                        %mi st
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %msubsup
                        %mi K
                        %mo *
                        %mi alg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_*^{st}(X, \mathbf{Z}/n) \simeq K_*^{alg}(X, \mathbf{Z}/n)
              %p
                while the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
                only sees the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
                of the variety and not the finer algebraic structure.
            %li
              %p
                Rationally, semi-topological K-theory contains information about the cycles on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+filtration"} Hodge filtration
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+cohomology"} singular cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi K
                        %mn 0
                        %mi st
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_0^{st}(X)
                coincides with the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group"} Grothendieck group
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
                up to
                = succeed "." do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    algebraic equivalence
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/algebraic+equivalence"} ?
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
                map induces canonical isomorphisms
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi K
                        %mn 0
                        %mi st
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ∼
                      %msubsup
                        %mi CH
                        %mi alg
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_0^{st}(X, \mathbf{Q}) \stackrel{\sim}{\longrightarrow} CH^*_alg(X, \mathbf{Q}),
              %p
                where on the right hand side is the group of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+cycles"} algebraic cycles
                modulo
                = succeed "." do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    algebraic equivalence
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/algebraic+equivalence"} ?
          %h2#references References
          %p
            A first definition of semi-topological K-theory for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+varieties"} complex varieties
            was given in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+M.+Friedlander"} Eric M. Friedlander
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Mark E. Walker
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Mark+E.+Walker"} ?
              = succeed "," do
                %em Semi-topological K-theory using function complexes
          %p
            An analogue of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-Hirzebruch+spectral+sequence"} Atiyah-Hirzebruch spectral sequence
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+M.+Friedlander"}> Eric M. Friedlander
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Christian Haesemeyer
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Christian+Haesemeyer"} ?
              = succeed "." do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Mark E. Walker
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Mark+E.+Walker"} ?
              = succeed "," do
                %em Techniques, computations, and conjectures for semi-topological K-theory
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0621/"} web
          %p A survey is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+M.+Friedlander"}> Eric M. Friedlander
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Mark E. Walker
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Mark+E.+Walker"} ?
              = succeed "," do
                %em Semi-topological K-theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+K-theory"} Handbook of K-theory
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.illinois.edu/K-theory/handbook/"} web
          %p
            Semi-topological K-theory for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-categories"} dg-categories
            was introduced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+Toen"} Bertrand Toen
            in lecture III of
          %ul
            %li#Toen10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+Toen"}> Bertrand Toen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Saturated dg-categories
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://math.berkeley.edu/~auroux/frg/miami10-notes/"} notes
          %p Some discussion and interesting conjectures are in the last section of
          %ul
            %li#Kaledin10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D.+Kaledin"}> D. Kaledin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Motivic structures in non-commutative geometry
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1003.3210"} arXiv:1003.3210
          %p
            A state of the art treatment via
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-categories"} dg-categories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+noncommutative+algebraic+geometry"} derived noncommutative algebraic geometry
          %ul
            %li#Blanc13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anthony+Blanc"}> Anthony Blanc
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological K-theory of complex noncommutative spaces
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1211.7360"} arXiv:1211.7360
        .revisedby
